def compute_baq(rec, refseq, extended=False):
    """BAQ approximation.

    Full BAQ uses a pair-HMM of the read against the reference to estimate,
    for each base, Phred-scaled probability that the base is misaligned.
    This implementation performs a banded forward-backward pair-HMM
    alignment (match/insert/delete states) and returns
    -10*log10(P(base is not aligned to the reference base implied by the
    read's CIGAR)).  It is a from-scratch model; values are close in spirit
    to samtools BAQ but may not be byte-identical in every case.
